<speak>The funny thing is that the quieter part of the day keeps moving. Previously, after lunch was peaceful. Now the warehouse supervisor comes back then, and everybody wants a discussion. I have started keeping a little block of time before I leave the office, just to collect my own papers and answer personal messages. Otherwise the papers go into my work bag and come home with me, and then my wife asks whether I am running the whole office from the dining table. She is quite right. I do not want our home to become another branch of the warehouse administration.</speak>